# --------------------- gwf swi options ---------------------
# mf6 subpackage utl-tvg

block options
name zeta_filerecord
type record zeta fileout zetafile
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description

block options
name zeta
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname zeta keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to zeta.

block options
name fileout
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname file keyword
description keyword to specify that an output filename is expected next.

block options
name zetafile
type string
preserve_case true
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged false
optional false
longname file keyword
description name of the binary output file to write zeta information.  This zeta output file has the same format as the binary heads file.

block options
name tvg6_filerecord
type record tvg6 filein tvg6_filename
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description

block options
name tvg6
type keyword
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname grid package component
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to a time varying grid array input file.

block options
name filein
type keyword
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname file keyword
description keyword to specify that an input filename is expected next.

block options
name tvg6_filename
type string
preserve_case true
in_record true
reader urword
tagged false
optional false
longname file keyword
description name of the time varying grid array input file.  The TVG file is a generic file for inputting time varying array data.  If the TVG file is specified in the options block, then the provided TVG file must have a SALTWATER\_HEAD auxiliary variable.  This SALTWATER\_HEAD auxiliary variable, which can vary during the simulation, will be assigned as the saltwater head used by the SWI Package. During solution of the freshwater flow equation, the provided SALTWATER\_HEAD array will remain fixed.  A common use case for providing SALTWATER\_HEAD in a TVG input file is to specify a sea level elevation that changes with time.  A description for the format of the TVG file is provided in a separate section.  If not specified, then the saltwater head will be set to zero, or to the saltwater\_head value that can be specified here as an option.

block options
name saltwater_head
type double precision
reader urword
optional true
longname saltwater head
description specified saltwater head value.  This saltwater head value will be assigned as the saltwater head used by the SWI Package. During solution of the freshwater flow equation the specified saltwater head will remain fixed.  A common use case for providing saltwater head is to set it equal to sea level, provided that sea level is not zero and does not change with time.  If not specified, and the TVG input option is not specified, then the default value for saltwater head is zero.  If the saltwater head option is specified and TVG input is also provided, then the TVG input will override the saltwater head option.
mf6internal hsalt_user

block options
name relative_density_difference
type double precision
reader urword
optional true
longname relative density difference
description dimensionless density difference between saltwater and freshwater, calculated as the saltwater density minus the freshwater density, divided by the freshwater density.  The value must be greater than zero.  If not specified, the default value is 0.025, which corresponds to a freshwater density of 1000. and a saltwater density of 1025.  The SWI Package uses this single dimensionless value instead of two densities because the interface position depends only on their ratio.  For a two-fluid simulation the same value must be specified for the freshwater model and the saltwater model; the SWI-SWI Exchange terminates with an error if the two differ.
mf6internal reldensdiff

